# Cloudflare Pages already serves /privacy from privacy.html natively and
# 308-redirects /privacy.html -> /privacy. The old "/privacy /privacy.html 200"
# rewrites fought that and produced an INFINITE REDIRECT LOOP on every legal
# page. App Review clicks those URLs. Do not reintroduce them.

# App Review and ad platforms both look for these exact paths
/privacy-policy  /privacy  301
/tos             /terms    301
/play            /play/    301

# /t/<code> and /c/<code> are Pages Functions, NOT redirect rules.
# Cloudflare does not substitute :splat inside a query string — the old
# `/t/* /play/?c=:splat 302` rule sent every shared invite to a literal
# ":splat" and silently broke the join-a-table loop. See functions/t/[code].js.
